## 10. Potential Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|------|----------|------------|
| **Behavioral divergence between `extractAll` and `extractImports`** | High | Phase 4 already has a side-by-side equivalence test that runs both pipelines on identical input and asserts identical output. This test will continue to run. |
| **lineCount difference** | Medium | The TypeScript parser uses `content.split(/\r?\n/).length` which counts trailing newlines differently. This was already validated and fixed in Phase 3. The equivalence test in `extractAll.test.ts` catches regressions. |
| **Parse error message format difference** | Medium | The legacy pipeline joins TS diagnostics with `"; "`. The new pipeline produces `IRParseError` objects with individual messages. `toLegacyResult()` joins them with `"; "` identically. Validated by existing tests. |
| **`ProjectFile` → `ParseFileInput` conversion error** | Low | The conversion is a trivial property rename (`filePath` → `relativePath`). TypeScript's type system will catch any mismatches at compile time. |
| **Registry not disposed on error** | Low | `disposeAll()` is in a `finally` block. The `LanguageParser` contract specifies that `dispose()` never throws. |
| **`discoverSourceFiles` returns `ProjectFile[]` but pipeline expects `ParseFileInput[]`** | Low | The explicit conversion step makes this visible and type-safe. |
| **`buildRepositoryIR` signature change breaks callers** | Low | Only one caller exists (`analyzeRepository.ts`), and it's being modified in the same change. |

